// CHAPTER 1
// ==========================================

= The Crust is Toast

#chapter_info(
  focus: "Physical Geography, Natural Disasters",
  plot: "Earth is doomed. The decision to flee."
)
The **atmosphere** inside the conference room was heavier than the **smog** outside. Dr. Aris pointed desperately at the holographic **globe** spinning in the center of the room.

"Mr. Husk, please look at the data," Aris pleaded. "The **lithosphere** is cracking. We are detecting abnormal **seismic** activity from the **Equator** to the **Antarctic**. This isn't just a **mishap**; it is a **catastrophic** event in the making."

Leon Husk, busy playing with a magnetic **pebble** he found on his private **beach**, didn't look up. "Aris, you worry too much. Is it just another **El Nino** **phenomenon**? Or maybe a seasonal **monsoon**?"

"No!" Aris shouted, slamming his hand on the table. "The **core** of the Earth is unstable! The **magma** is rising through the **mantle** and pressing against the **crust**. We are looking at a global **calamity**. Yesterday, a **volcano** that has been **dormant** for centuries suddenly **erupted** in the **Pacific** Ocean. It caused a **tsunami** that swallowed an entire **peninsula**!"

Leon finally paused. "A tsunami? Did it hit my factory?"

"Forget the factory! The **terrain** is changing. **glaciers** are melting at an **unprecedented** rate, causing **flooding** in the low-lying **plains**. Meanwhile, the **interior** of the **continent** is suffering from severe **drought**. The **landscape** is turning into a **barren** **desert**. If we don't leave, we will be buried under **debris** and **sediment**."

Leon stood up and walked to the window. Outside, a **gale** was blowing, and a **downpour** of acidic rain obscured the **horizon**. The **climate** had indeed **deteriorated**.

"Okay," Leon said, his eyes gleaming with a **spark** of madness. "If the **terrestrial** environment is **toxic**, we go up. Prepare the **spacecraft**. We need to reach a safe **altitude** before the **typhoon** hits."

"You mean... leave Earth?" Aris asked, trembling.

"Yes," Leon grinned. "We are going to explore the **cosmos**. I heard Mars has a nice **valley** view this time of year. Plus, no **hurricanes** there."

Aris looked at the **lightning** flashing across the **stormy** sky. It was a **dilemma**, but sticking around for the **avalanche** of doom seemed like a bad idea.

"Fine," Aris sighed. "But we need to calculate the **orbit** precisely. One wrong move, and we burn up in the **atmosphere**."
