= The Gizmo that Saved the World

#chapter_info(
  focus: "Technology, Items & Materials, Fashion",
  plot: "The ship breaks down. Repairing high-tech gear with style."
)

**Location:** The Main Engineering Deck of "The Ark".

It was a Tuesday (probably), and Leon decided it was time to launch his new **interstellar** **fashion** brand.

"Aris, look at me!" Leon twirled in the center of the control room. He was wearing a **tight**, shiny **silver** **outfit** made of **synthetic** **fiber**. It featured a high **collar**, long **sleeves** **adorned** with fake **gems** and **beads**, and a massive, flowing **velvet** **cape**. "I call this look 'The Cosmic King'. It’s going to be the new **vogue**. A total **trend**."

Aris, who was busy trying to **calculate** the ship's fuel consumption using a **digital** **gauge**, didn't look up. "Leon, that **costume** looks **ridiculous**. It’s not **stylish**; it looks like you wrapped yourself in **aluminum foil** (foil不在表里，用**metal**代替) **metal** sheets."

"You have no taste for **luxury** or **elegance**," Leon scoffed, adjusting his **belt**. "This is **high-definition** beauty. My **fans** on Earth are watching this on the **wireless** **network**. I am their **icon**, their **idol**."

Leon walked over to the main **ventilation** unit to pose for the **camera**. "Look at the **texture** of this **fabric**," he bragged, leaning against the **intake** **fan**.

Suddenly, disaster struck.

A **gust** of air sucked the hem of Leon's **velvet** **cape** into the spinning **blades** of the fan. _ZZZZT! CRACK!_

The **fan** jammed. The **motor** screeched. Sparks flew from the **switch** board.

"My cape!" Leon shrieked. "The ship!" Aris yelled.

Red lights flashed on the **screen**. A robotic voice announced: _"Critical **error**. **Ventilation** system failure. **Oxygen** **circulation** stopped. **Hydraulic** **pressure** dropping."_

"You broke the air scrubber!" Aris panicked. He rushed to the **emergency** **cabinet** and grabbed a **kit** full of **tools**. "I need to fix this before we suffocate!"

"Well, hurry up!" Leon demanded, trying to untangle his **shredded** cape. "This is a **fashion** emergency! My **image** is being ruined!"

Aris ignored him. He needed to be a **mechanic** now, not a geologist. He opened the machine's **shutter** and peered inside. It was a **mess**. The **cape** had tangled around the main **gear** and the **pivot**. The **friction** had caused the **rubber** **belt** to snap.

"I need materials!" Aris shouted. "Leon, bring me the **spare** parts **box** from the **storage**!"

Leon ran and came back with a **bin** full of **junk**: old **cables**, a **broken** **toaster**, a **plastic** **bucket**, and a **tube** of **glue**.

"This is **garbage**!" Aris cried. "I need a **wrench** or a **screwdriver**!"

"Use your imagination! **Improvise**!" Leon said unhelpfully.

Aris took a deep breath. He had to **devise** a solution. He saw a loose **bolt** and a rusted **screw**. He used a metal **spoon** (from his lunch) as a lever to pry open the **casing**. He found the broken **circuit**.

"I need to **connect** these wires," Aris muttered. He stripped the **insulation** off a **cord** using a pair of **scissors**. He realized he didn't have soldering **equipment**, so he used a piece of **gum** (Leon was chewing it) to stick the wires together temporarily. "It's a crude **technique**, but it might work."

Next, the **gear**. It was stuck. "I need **lubricant**!" Leon handed him a bottle of expensive **shampoo**. "It's silky smooth." "Fine!" Aris poured the **shampoo** onto the **gear**. It became slippery. He grabbed the tangled **fabric** and pulled. _Rip!_ The cape came free.

Finally, the snapped **belt**. Aris looked at Leon. "Give me your **leather** **belt**." "What? This is genuine Italian **leather**! It cost a fortune!" "Give it to me, or we die!" Leon sighed and handed it over. Aris used a **knife** to trim the **edge**, punched a hole with a **nail**, and wrapped it around the **wheel**.

He flipped the **switch**. _Whirrrr..._

The **fan** started to spin. The **generator** hummed. The red warning light on the **monitor** turned green. Fresh air began to **circulate** again.

Aris collapsed on the **floor**, wiping **grease** and **sweat** from his forehead with a **rag**. He looked at his **shabby**, oil-stained clothes.

Leon stood up, smoothing his torn **garment**. "Well," he said, looking at the camera. "As I was saying... this **distressed** look is the latest **trend**. It symbolizes the **fragile** nature of human existence."

Aris threw the **wrench** (imaginary wrench) at him.
