= The Great Space Jam

#chapter_info(
  focus: "Entertainment & Sports, Art & Music",
  plot: "Boredom strikes. Zero-gravity Olympics."
)

**Location:** The Cargo Bay (converted into a "Multipurpose Stadium").

"Welcome, **ladies and gentlemen**—and mutant goats!" Leon’s voice boomed over the **loudspeaker**. He was standing on a floating platform, holding a **microphone**. "Today, we make history. Welcome to the first annual Ark **Olympic** Games!"

Aris floated into the room, looking tired. "Leon, there are only two of us. How can we have a **competition**?"

"Details, details," Leon waved his hand. "We need **recreation**. We need to maintain our **physical** **fitness**. Plus, the Lio-sheep is an excellent **athlete**. Look at those muscles."

Leon pointed to the mutant lion-sheep, which was currently chewing on a **volleyball** net.

"First event: Zero-Gravity **Tennis**!" Leon announced. He tossed a **racket** to Aris. "The rules are simple. You hit the ball over the net. If you **drift** into the ceiling, you lose a point."

Aris sighed but grabbed the **racket**. He missed **exercise**. He tried to **serve**, throwing the ball up. But in zero-G, the ball didn't come down. It just **hovered** there. Leon seized the moment, swung his racket, and performed a violent **smash**. The ball flew past Aris, bounced off the wall, hit a **drum** kit in the corner, and landed in Leon's hand.

"Point to me!" Leon shouted. "I am the **champion**! The crowd goes wild!" He pressed a button, and a recording of **cheering** **spectators** played loudly.

Next came the **marathon**. Since they couldn't run far, Leon set up two treadmills. "We will **jog** in place for four hours," Leon said. "Keep a steady **pace** and maintain your **rhythm**."

Ten minutes later, Leon got bored. "This is dull. Let's switch to the Arts **Festival**."

He dimmed the lights and turned on a **spotlight**. "Behold, my **gallery**."

He pulled a sheet off a pile of twisted metal, broken wires, and old food wrappers. "I call this **sculpture** _'The Agony of a Lost Wi-Fi Signal'_. It is a masterpiece of **abstract** **art**. Notice the **aesthetic** balance between the **garbage** and the **void**."

Aris stared at the pile of trash. "It looks like a broken **toaster** stuck to a **shoe**."

"You are no **critic**," Leon scoffed. "You lack **artistic** vision. Now, prepare yourself for the highlight of the evening: The **Concert**."

Leon floated over to a collection of instruments he had **improvised** from spare ship parts. There was a "guitar" made of a shovel and rubber bands, and a "drum" made of empty water tanks.

"I will now **perform** a **solo**," Leon announced. "It is a fusion of **classical**, **jazz**, **rock**, and **hip-hop**. I call it 'Space Noise'."

He started to play. It was loud. It was chaotic. There was no **melody**, no **tune**, and certainly no **harmony**. He banged on the **drum** while screaming unintelligible **lyrics** into the mic.


"Listen to that **rhythm**!" Leon yelled, strumming his shovel-guitar. "I am a musical **genius**! I am better than any **band** on Earth! I am the new **Pop** King!"

The Lio-sheep, unable to bear the noise, let out a deafening **roar** that sounded surprisingly like a **trumpet**.

"Ah," Leon stopped playing. "The **audience** is participating! A true **symphony** of nature and machine!"

Aris floated over to the **piano** (which was actually just a keyboard painted on a table). "Leon, please. Let's just watch a **movie**. Do we have any **films** in the database?"

"Fine," Leon pouted, putting down his shovel. "But nothing boring. I want action, **drama**, **comedy**, and **tragedy** all in one."

They settled down to watch an old **animation**. But as the opening credits rolled, Aris noticed something strange on the screen.

"Leon," Aris pointed. "Why is the **conductor** of the **orchestra** in the movie wearing a gas mask?"

Leon froze. "Wait. That's not the movie. That's a reflection." He sniffed the air. "Do you smell burning plastic?"

"You overloaded the **circuits** with your electric shovel!" Aris screamed. "The kitchen **fuse** just blew!"

"Well," Leon shrugged. "At least the **show** ended with a bang."

