= Mars BnB

#chapter_info(
  focus: "Architecture, Transport/Travel",
  plot: "Landing on Mars. Building the base."
)

**Location:** The Surface of Mars (Utopia Planitia).

"Attention, **passengers**," Leon announced over the intercom, even though Aris was sitting right next to him. "We are approaching our **destination**. Please fasten your seatbelts and stow your **luggage** in the overhead **rack**. We may experience a slight **delay** due to a dust storm on the **route**."

The **shuttle** (a smaller **vehicle** detached from The Ark) shook violently as it entered the thin Martian atmosphere.

"Leon, slow down!" Aris yelled. "You are coming in too fast! The **landing** gear won't hold!"

"Relax," Leon grinned, steering with one hand. "I’m an excellent **pilot**. I’m aiming for that flat **site** near the **canyon**. It’s the perfect location for a **resort**."

_BOOM!_

The shuttle slammed into the red dust, bounced twice, and skidded to a **halt** near a pile of rocks.

"We have **arrived**," Leon said, dusting off his jacket. "Welcome to Mars **Harbour**. Please check that you haven't left any personal items on the **craft**."

They stepped out. The **landscape** was desolate but majestic.

"Okay," Leon clapped his hands. "Time to **construct** our new home. Aris, unload the 'Instant-City' modules from the **cargo** hold."

Aris dragged out several heavy crates. "We need a basic **shelter** first. A secure **dwelling** to protect us from radiation and cold. Maybe a small **hut** or a **cabin**."

"Think bigger, Aris!" Leon pressed a button on a remote. "I didn't travel 140 million miles to live in a **shed**. I'm building a **villa**."

One of the crates exploded open. Nanobots swarmed out, assembling materials. In minutes, a structure began to rise. It wasn't a simple base; it was a monstrosity.

It had a grand **entrance** with tall **marble** **columns** (fake marble, actually plastic). It had a **lobby** with a crystal **chandelier** (which didn't sparkle because there was no light). It even had a **balcony** overlooking the dusty **plain**.

"Behold!" Leon gestured. "The Musk Mansion. It features a spacious **living room**, a **master bedroom**, and a **guest** **suite** for you."

Aris walked inside. "Leon, this is ridiculous. Where is the **infrastructure**? Where is the **plumbing**? Where is the **sewage** system?"

"Details," Leon waved him off. "Check out the **elevator**. It goes up to the **terrace** on the roof."

"It's a two-**storey** building," Aris pointed out. "We can use the **stairs**."

"We also have a **commercial** wing," Leon continued. "Over there, I plan to build a **mall** and a **casino**. And maybe a **stadium** for the Lio-sheep to play **soccer**."

Aris inspected the **foundation**. It looked shaky. The **concrete** was setting too fast in the cold. "Leon, this **structure** is unstable. The **ceiling** is sagging. And you put the **toilet** in the **kitchen**!"

"It's an open-concept **layout**," Leon argued. "Very modern. Very **urban** style."

"We are in a **rural** desert!" Aris shouted. "We need a **warehouse** for food storage, a **greenhouse** for the plants, and a **power plant** for electricity. Instead, you built a **skyscraper** that is only two floors high!"

Suddenly, a warning siren wailed from the shuttle. _"Warning: Sandstorm approaching. **Visibility** zero."_

"Quick!" Aris pushed Leon inside. "Seal the **shutters**! Lock the **gate**!"

They huddled in the **corridor**, the safest place in the "mansion." The wind howled outside, battering the **walls** and **roof**.

"Well," Leon whispered in the dark. "At least the **location** is prime. Once the storm clears, the property value will skyrocket. We can rent out the spare **apartment** on Airbnb."

"Who are we going to rent it to?" Aris asked. "The aliens?"

"You never know," Leon smirked. "I put up a **signpost** near the landing zone. 'Vacancy. Free Wi-Fi.' They'll come."
