**Location:** The Grand Hall of the Musk Mansion (a.k.a. the living room).

The sun rose over the red horizon. Aris walked into the living room to find Leon sitting behind a desk, wearing a sash that said "Supreme Leader."

"Good morning, **citizen**," Leon said solemnly. "I have stayed up all night drafting the **Constitution**."

"The what?" Aris asked, yawning.

"The **Constitution** of the United **Republic** of Mars," Leon held up a piece of napkin with scribbles on it. "We need a formal **government** to maintain **order** and **stability**. I have appointed myself as the **President**, the **Prime Minister**, and the **Minister** of Defense."

"And what am I?" Aris asked.

"You are the **population**," Leon replied. "And also the **Vice** **Minister** of Sanitation (cleaning toilets). Congratulations on your **appointment**."

Aris rolled his eyes. "Leon, this isn't a **democracy**; it's a **dictatorship** (implied by **regime**). I demand an **election**."

"We can hold a **vote** later," Leon dismissed him. "But first, we must discuss the **economy**. Our **society** needs a **currency** to facilitate **trade**."

Leon opened a suitcase full of plastic chips. "I introduce to you: The Leon-Coin. It is the official **legal** tender of Mars."

"This is ridiculous," Aris said. "We don't need money. We just share resources."

"That sounds like **socialism**," Leon narrowed his eyes. "In my **capitalist** **system**, everything has a price. For example, I own the **infrastructure**, including the air scrubbers. Therefore, I am imposing a **tax** on oxygen."

"You can't **tax** air!" Aris shouted. "That violates my basic **human rights**!"

"I have the **authority**," Leon tapped a gavel (a hammer). "If you cannot pay, you will go into **debt**. But don't worry, the **Bank** of Leon offers **loans** with a very reasonable 50% **interest** rate."

Aris was furious. "I refuse to pay! I am going on **strike**!"

"Then you are breaking the **law**," Leon stood up. "I accuse you of **tax evasion** and **treason**. As the **police** chief, I hereby **arrest** you."

Leon tried to handcuff Aris with a zip-tie. Aris pushed him away.

"I demand a **trial**!" Aris yelled. "I want a **lawyer** and a **jury**!"

"Fine," Leon sat back down. "The **court** is now in **session**. I am the **judge**. The **jury** consists of the Lio-sheep and Gary the giant salamander."

"This **judicial** process is a joke," Aris protested. "You are the **plaintiff**, the **judge**, and the **witness**? There is no **justice** here! This is a **corrupt** **regime**!"

"Silence in the court!" Leon banged the table. "The **evidence** is clear. You consumed 500 liters of my oxygen without **payment**. The **verdict** is... **guilty**. Your **sentence** is hard **labor**—you must clean the solar panels for a month."

"I appeal!" Aris shouted. "I challenge your **legitimacy**. I hereby declare a **revolution**!"

Aris grabbed the bag of Leon-Coins and threw them out the window.

"My **capital**!" Leon screamed, watching his **wealth** scatter in the Martian wind. "You just caused hyper-**inflation**! The **market** will crash!"

"Power to the people!" Aris chanted. "I am organizing a **campaign** for a new leader."

"Fine!" Leon crossed his arms. "Let's vote. Who votes for me?" Leon raised his hand. "Who votes for Aris?" Aris raised his hand.

"It's a tie," Leon grumbled. "We have a **political** deadlock. The **parliament** is hung."

Suddenly, the Lio-sheep walked in, ate the **Constitution** (the napkin), and burped.

"I think the **supreme** **court** just overruled us both," Aris noted.

"Okay," Leon sighed, taking off his sash. "New **policy**. No taxes. But you still have to cook dinner. That's a **mandatory** **regulation**."

"Deal," Aris agreed. "But if you try to sell me water again, I will **sue** you.ed to mint coins. "This is the new #vocab("currency")," he said. Aris pointed out the #vocab("inflation") risks since there were no goods to buy.

