= The Mutiny

#chapter_info(
  focus: "War/Conflict, Actions",
  plot: "Mutant animals revolt. Action sequences."
)

**Location:** The Musk Mansion, Mars.

The morning started with an ominous silence. Aris walked into the kitchen and found the Lio-sheep standing on the table. It was **glaring** at him. Its eyes were no longer the eyes of a dumb beast; they were full of **hatred** and **intelligence**.

"Shoo!" Aris waved his hand. "Get down!"

The Lio-sheep didn't move. Instead, it let out a low **growl** (roar) that sounded like a **threat**. Suddenly, Gary the giant salamander kicked open the door. A **troop** of mutant chickens marched in, their beaks sharp as **blades**.

"Leon!" Aris **shouted**, backing away. "We have a problem!"

Leon rushed in, wearing his pajamas. "What is this **disturbance**? Why are you **interrupting** my beauty sleep?"

"It's a **revolt**!" Aris cried. "The animals are staging a **mutiny**!"

"Ridiculous," Leon **scoffed**. He walked up to the Lio-sheep. "Listen here, you **rebel**. I am your **general**, your creator! I **command** you to **cease** this behavior immediately!"

The Lio-sheep **snatched** Leon’s "Supreme Leader" sash with its teeth and ripped it apart. It was a clear act of **treason**.

"Okay," Leon whispered, his face pale. "That was **aggressive**. They are **hostile**. Aris, prepare for **battle**."

"With what?" Aris asked, **trembling** (shaking).

"We need **weapons**," Leon said. He ran to the closet and **equipped** himself with a tennis racket (now a **shield**) and a modified leaf-blower (now a **cannon**). He handed Aris a bottle of spicy sauce. "This is your **pistol**. Aim for the eyes."

The animals launched their **attack**. It was a **fierce** **assault**. The chickens fired **missiles** (eggs) with deadly accuracy. Gary the salamander used his tail to **smash** the furniture.

"Defend the perimeter!" Leon yelled, trying to **deter** the chickens with a blast of air. "Do not let them **invade** the living room!"

But the **enemy** had a **strategy**. While the chickens distracted them, the Lio-sheep led a **flank** attack (side attack) and **seized** the refrigerator.

"They captured the food supply!" Aris screamed. "This is a **catastrophe**! We will **starve**!"

"Do not **panic**!" Leon **roared**, trying to **rally** his courage. "We must **counter**\-attack! Charge!"

Leon **dashed** forward, swinging his racket. He tried to **strike** Gary, but the slippery amphibian **dodged** and **whipped** Leon’s legs. Leon **tumbled** (fell) to the ground.

"I am **wounded**!" Leon cried dramatically, holding his knee (which was just slightly **bruised**). "Aris, save me!"

Aris looked at the chaos. The room was in **turmoil**. The **violence** was escalating. He realized they couldn't **defeat** this army. The animals were too **sturdy** and **reckless**.

"We have to **retreat**!" Aris grabbed Leon by the collar and started to **drag** him. "Fall back to the greenhouse! It's our only **refuge**!"

They **fled** down the corridor, dodging flying eggs. The animals **pursued** them, **barking** and **hissing** in **triumph**.

Aris slammed the heavy glass door of the greenhouse and **locked** it. He **leaned** against it, panting. Outside, the Lio-sheep **stared** at them through the glass, a look of **victory** on its face. It had **conquered** the mansion.

"We are under **siege**," Leon gasped, looking at the army **surrounding** their glass prison. "They have cut off our supplies. It's a **conspiracy**. They planned this."

"Why?" Aris asked, wiping sweat from his brow. "Why did they **rebel**?"

Leon looked through the glass. The Lio-sheep was currently trying to turn on the TV.

"I think..." Leon muttered. "I think they just wanted to watch the cartoons we watched in Chapter 6. I **prohibited** them from watching TV last night."

"You started a **war** over cartoons?" Aris **glared** at him.

"I'm a **strict** parent," Leon shrugged. "But now, we are **destitute**. We are **prisoners** in our own ship. We have lost our **freedom**."

"We have to **negotiate**," Aris said, holding up a white towel (a sign of **surrender**). "We have to **compromise**."

Leon sighed. "Fine. I will **offer** them Netflix password. But I refuse to **bow** to a sheep."
