= Reflections on Time

#chapter_info(
  focus: "Time, Emotions/Abstract",
  plot: "Reflection and nostalgia."
)

**Location:** Inside the Greenhouse, looking out at the Martian night sky.

It was **midnight**. Or maybe it was **midday**. It was hard to tell. On Mars, the **daily** cycle was slightly longer than on Earth, throwing their biological clock into chaos.

Leon sat on a sack of fertilizer, staring at the stars. His usual **energetic** and **hectic** **mood** had vanished. He looked **gloomy**, **miserable**, and strangely **quiet**.

"Aris," Leon broke the **silence**. "Do you know what date it is?"

"I've lost track," Aris sighed, checking his watch. "The **battery** died a **century** ago. Or maybe just a week. Time feels **everlasting** here. It stretches out into an infinite **duration**."

"On Earth," Leon whispered, "it would be the **anniversary** of my company's founding. Usually, I would be hosting an **annual** gala. There would be **music**, **laughter**, and **champagne**. I would be the **center** of attention, looking **confident** and **proud**."

He looked down at his torn clothes. "Now, look at me. I look **wretched** and **awkward**. My **reputation** is ruined. I bet the **contemporary** media is calling me a **failure**. They probably think I'm **insane** or **mad**."

Aris looked at Leon. For the first time, he didn't feel **anger** or **hatred**. He felt **sympathetic**.

"Leon," Aris said gently. "You are **arrogant**, **selfish**, and **stubborn**. You are often a **nuisance** and a **bother**. But you are also **enterprising**. You dared to come here. That is not **negligible**."

Leon managed a weak smile. "You are being **frank**."

"I'm being **honest**," Aris sat next to him. "Initially, I was **reluctant** to come. I was **hesitant** and **skeptical**. I felt **resentment** (bitterness) towards you. But in the **midst** of all this chaos, I realized something. We are living in a new **era**."

"A **medieval** era," Leon grumbled. "Ruled by chickens."

"Perhaps," Aris chuckled. "But think about it. We are the **foremost** humans on this planet. Every **moment** we survive is a **precedent**. We are creating history **simultaneously** with our suffering."

Leon looked out the glass. The Lio-sheep was sleeping near the door. The **hostile** atmosphere had temporarily calmed down.

"I feel **guilty**," Leon confessed, his voice **trembling**. "I was **greedy**. I wanted **fame** and **fortune**. I was **indifferent** to the risks. I **ignored** your warnings. I was **rash** and **reckless**. Now, I **regret** everything. I am **ashamed**."

Aris patted his shoulder. "Don't **weep**, Leon. It's **useless** to **mourn** the past. The **former** world is behind us. We have to focus on the **present** and the **imminent** future."

"Do you think we have a future?" Leon asked, sounding **pessimistic** and **desperate**. "The animals are **sturdy** and **vicious**. Our situation is **unstable**."

"I am **optimistic**," Aris said, pointing at a small blue dot in the sky. "Look. That's Earth. It looks so **peaceful**, so **delicate**. It reminds me that our problems are **temporary**. We just need to be **patient** and **rational**."

Leon gazed at the pale blue dot. A wave of **nostalgia** (homesickness) washed over him. He felt a deep **yearning** for home.

"You are right," Leon wiped his eyes. "I shouldn't be **passive**. I need to be **positive**. I need to regain my **zeal**. We will survive this."

"**Incidentally**," Aris added. "I think the Lio-sheep likes music. Remember the concert? It stopped attacking when you played the **rhythm**. Maybe we can tame them."

Leon's eyes lit up. His **enthusiastic** **personality** returned **immediately**.

"Music!" Leon jumped up. "Of course! I am a musical **genius**! I will compose a **symphony** of peace! It will be **glorious**! It will be **awesome**!"

Aris smiled. The old, annoying Leon was back. But this time, Aris felt a sense of **mutual** understanding. They were partners in this **ridiculous** fate.

"Okay, Mozart," Aris stood up. "Let's wait for **dawn**. Tomorrow, we negotiate with the chickens. But for the **meantime**, let's get some sleep."

"Goodnight, Aris," Leon said, sounding **sincere**. "And... thank you. For being **tolerant**."

"Goodnight, Mr. President," Aris replied.

Outside, the wind howled, but inside, there was finally a sense of **harmony**.
